{
  "id": "qra1-l13",
  "world": "qra1",
  "source": "DHM Quran Recitation (QRA1) · lesson 13. From Dr. Hassan's course; every word in his voice, every verse by Sheikh Al-Minshawi.",
  "title": {
    "ar": "تَنْوِينُ الْفَتْحِ",
    "en": "Tanween with fatha"
  },
  "topic": "Read tanween with fatha and recite Surat Al-Humazah",
  "minutes": 15,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "Tanween adds an “n” sound at the end of a word. We say it, but we don't write the noon. It is written as double short vowels and comes only at the end of nouns.",
      "title": "Tanween"
    },
    {
      "en": "Two fathas on the last letter, usually followed by an alif that is written but not said. The sound is “an”.",
      "title": "Tanween with fatha"
    },
    {
      "en": "Now we read the name of the surah.",
      "title": "The surah",
      "ar": "سُورَةُ الْهُمَزَةِ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar",
      "tr": "soorato alhomazate"
    },
    {
      "en": "Listen to Sheikh Al-Minshawi recite Surat Al-Humazah. Follow with your finger, then recite it yourself.",
      "title": "Surat Al-Humazah",
      "ar": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ وَيْلٌۭ لِّكُلِّ هُمَزَةٍۢ لُّمَزَةٍ ﴿١﴾ ٱلَّذِى جَمَعَ مَالًۭا وَعَدَّدَهُۥ ﴿٢﴾ يَحْسَبُ أَنَّ مَالَهُۥٓ أَخْلَدَهُۥ ﴿٣﴾ كَلَّا ۖ لَيُنۢبَذَنَّ فِى ٱلْحُطَمَةِ ﴿٤﴾ وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا ٱلْحُطَمَةُ ﴿٥﴾ نَارُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُوقَدَةُ ﴿٦﴾ ٱلَّتِى تَطَّلِعُ عَلَى ٱلْأَفْـِٔدَةِ ﴿٧﴾ إِنَّهَا عَلَيْهِم مُّؤْصَدَةٌۭ ﴿٨﴾ فِى عَمَدٍۢ مُّمَدَّدَةٍۭ ﴿٩﴾",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "At the end of any gathering, the Prophet ﷺ advised us to say this du'aa: Glory is to You, O Allah, and praise. We bear witness that none has the right to be worshiped except You. We seek Your forgiveness and we turn to You in repentance.",
      "title": "At the end of our lesson",
      "ar": "سُبْحَانَكَ اللَّهُمَّ وَبِحَمْدِكَ، نَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا أَنْتَ، نَسْتَغْفِرُكَ وَنَتُوبُ إِلَيْكَ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar",
      "tr": "Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, nashhadu an la ilaha illa anta, nastaghfiruka wa natubu ilayk"
    }
  ],
